WEBVTT

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:56.170
Bottom Flap

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.360
<i>Cut!</i>

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.690
Okay, camera rehearsal looks good.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:10.950
You two, I told you boys to 
stop looking at the camera.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.520
Girl carrying the dog and you two 
on the bike, you're too slow.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.980
You two walking and eating sweet 
rolls, don't eat before a take.

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.370
This will be a take.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:30.380
It was supposed to be just 
a little independent film.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.470
Feel this in your soul!

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:34.640
<i>Nobody expected it to turn into 
such a grand undertaking.</i>

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:40.210
<i>It started one week ago.</i>

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.590
A blood drive PV?

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:51.830
I believe posters and fliers 
aren't nearly appealing enough.

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.630
In order to reach the entire 
student body, we need a video.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:59.810
Not just a banal PR video, 
but a properly entertaining one.

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.850
That sounds kind of fun.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:07.220
Naturally, it shall be 
produced by the Cinema Club.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.050
Will we be involved?

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:12.850
We would appreciate the Cosplay and 
Dance Club's full cooperation.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:15.020
Sounds like a pain in the ass.

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:19.290
You'd better not fool around like 
you did during the school festival.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.740
You're one to talk.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.300
I get the gist of it.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.770
But if you're going to make a movie, 
there are a few things you'll need first.

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:31.610
Even if you don't pay the cast or staff 
and use the Cinema Club's equipment,

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:36.910
there're transportation fees, lunch 
fees, beverages, and a snack bar.

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:38.310
And if you're planning on 
releasing it to the public,

00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:41.460
the studio fees required to put on the 
finishing touches are nothing to sneeze at.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:43.810
I've already come up with an estimate.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:49.460
We'll spend two weeks filming, and the 
total cost comes out to 482,520 yen.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.100
480,000 yen?

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.990
Where are we going to 
find that kind of money?

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.730
Pie in the sky. Castles in the air.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:58.760
This is ridiculous.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.760
Just so you know, I don't 
intend to pay a single cent.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.700
Thanks for waiting.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.290
How did it go?

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:11.960
500,000 rounded up. 
I had everyone pay in full.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.350
<b>500K Yen</b>

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:13.790
What?!

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:16.480
Where did that idiot get that much money?

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.150
I bet it was extortion.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.600
That's a crime.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.550
Then he robbed a bank.

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:25.760
Rumor is, Katsuno's actually 
the son of a wealthy family.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.160
He got it from daddy.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.370
What are you squabbling about?

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:33.300
I earned this money with my 
blood, sweat, and fists.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.160
So it was extortion after all.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:38.830
This means I get to play 
Mai-chan's boyfriend, right?

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:40.830
A director never goes back on her word.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:41.300
<b>Lie</b>

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:41.920
<b>Lie</b>

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:41.920
<b>Lie</b>

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:42.510
<b>Lie</b>

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:42.510
<b>Lie</b>

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:42.510
<b>Lie</b>

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.130
<b>Lie</b>

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.130
<b>Lie</b>

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.130
<b>Lie</b>

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.130
<b>Lie</b>

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:47.550
Anyway, we've met the conditions 
required for production.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.700
Doctor Chihiro, as the Blood Donation 
Club advisor and night school supervisor,

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.390
I ask for your permission.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:53.930
Very well.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:58.870
However, I'm only canceling night 
classes for five days so you can film.

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:00.090
That's ridiculous!

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.920
There's nothing ridiculous about it.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.570
"If you can't finish shooting in five days, 
you wouldn't finish shooting in five years."

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.830
A certain movie director once said that.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:07.820
<b>Inu</b>

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:11.810
Well, whatever. Once filming starts, 
a movie belongs to its director.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.540
<b>Naive</b>

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:19.260
I'll now go over the staff and cast list.

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:23.090
Meet Mai (Temp)

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:23.240
Leading lady Dracula will be 
played by Mai Vlad Transylvania.

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.240
I look forward to working with everyone.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:27.580
Her fiancé will be played by Mitsugu Bambam.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:29.860
<i>That's to be expected.</i>

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:33.900
Mitsugu's senior who elopes with Mai 
will be played by Masumi Katsuno.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.790
It's the only thing to do.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.660
Costumes, Kaoru Konno.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:40.300
The Cosplay Club is finally up at bat again.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.340
Dance instruction, Nami Unten.

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:44.470
Better than attending classes.

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:46.730
Production manager, Jinko Sumida.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:49.270
Stick to the schedule. Discipline on set.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:52.500
Executive producer, 
Doctor Chihiro Chimatsuri.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:57.860
The Cinema Club will devote 
all its energies to direction,

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:24.270
Meet Mai (Temp)

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:00.360
and production will be handled by 
the Karate Club and all the rest.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:05.090
And I, Maki Watabe, shall be the director.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:10.040
We start shooting one week from now, 
and we'll begin preparing today.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.170
Roger!

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:22.970
<i>Thus, amidst uncertainty and doubt, 
the production of Maki's movie began.</i>

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:27.190
FIRST DAY OF SHOOTING

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:40.450
Katsuno-senpai of the Blood Donation Club,

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:43.300
allow me to introduce our new member Mai.

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:44.960
Cut!

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.670
Okay. This will be a take.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:49.360
Okay.

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.030
Hey, listen.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:52.300
Oh, what a surprise.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:55.230
What's going on with this movie's script?

00:06:55.230 --> 00:07:00.670
Since we only have five days to film, 
we'll improvise and fix it in editing.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:05.490
All that exists is what we're shooting 
that day, Jackie Chan-style.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.940
But we don't even have today's script.

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:10.520
We do. It's right in here.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:12.020
Even if I gave you a script,

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:15.420
it's not like you have the ability to come 
up with an acting plan or prepare for the role.

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:16.840
Yeah, but...

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:18.650
There's more?

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:23.020
I feel like I've seen this 
situation before somewhere.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:25.490
I'm surprised you've seen it.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:32.630
<b>Day for Night</b>

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:32.410
It's from the 1973 French 
movie <i>Day for Night</i>

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.630
directed by François Truffaut.

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:37.860
The guy who played the scientist in 
<i>Close Encounters of the Third Kind</i>?

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:39.180
<b>Close Encounters
of the Third Kind</b>

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:41.770
He's also an actor, but he's also one of 
the great masters of the French New Wave.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:44.840
Though the movie primarily 
takes place on film sets,

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:49.570
<b>Day for Night</b>

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:47.110
it's a masterpiece that's a little different

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:49.230
from your standard Hollywood 
behind-the-scenes movie.

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:52.860
It stars English actress Jacqueline Bisset

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:57.530
and handsome French actor Jean-Pierre 
Léaud, who often worked with Godard.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:01.910
And the director in the movie 
is played by Truffaut himself.

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:05.800
By the way, the English title <i>Day for Night</i>

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:08.470
refers to the cinematic technique of using filters

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:10.620
to block out warm-colored light for night scenes.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:13.510
I wasn't asking about that.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:20.840
The movie being shot within the film is a 
cliché melodrama called <i>Meet Pamela</i>.

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:24.520
<b>Meet Pamela</b>

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:21.570
In other words...

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:24.570
I'm paying homage to that movie.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:27.400
<b>Meet Mai</b>

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.880
So the title of this movie 
will be <i>Meet Mai</i>.

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:30.450
Oh, I see—no, wait. 
I wasn't asking about that.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:31.770
There's no point in telling you.

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:35.210
In the first place, isn't this movie 
supposed to promote the blood drive?

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:41.180
Regardless of the subject of the movie, 
the director needs a personal theme.

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:44.100
I'm a cinemaphile full of love for movies.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.450
We're on standby.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.700
This is a take.

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:48.280
Katsuno!

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:50.960
This is the scene where you and the heroine

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.480
meet that foreshadows your eventual elopement.

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:56.030
It's the only thing to do!

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:56.920
This is a take.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:02.090
<i>Meet Mai</i> scene number unknown, 
cut number unknown. Take one.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.220
Ready, action!

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.840
Katsuno-senpai, allow me to 
introduce our new member Mai.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:15.440
Cut!

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:17.930
Camera B, are you getting 
that closeup of Katsuno?

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.570
Katsuno's missing.

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:20.190
What?

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:22.610
Take this!

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:24.460
I'm taking you with me!

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.910
He kidnapped Mai?!

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.580
After them!

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:34.300
That won't be necessary. Click.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:40.470
<b>Censored</b>

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:43.010
Captain!

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:46.540
I installed an anti-theft 
self-destruct spark plug.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:50.280
Doctor, you installed 
that in your own moped?

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.300
What if Mai is dead?

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:56.040
That girl isn't that fragile.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:01.990
Since my moped was well-insured,

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:04.960
starting next week I'll be 
riding a brand new moped.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:07.540
Miraculously, Katsuno survived,

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:13.300
* Insurance fraud is a crime.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.310
but there was no trace of the 
Vespa we'd been using to film,

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:13.290
and thus, the first day of shooting concluded.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:16.220
SECOND DAY OF SHOOTING

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:20.150
<i>Maki pulled herself together, 
announced that starting today,</i>

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:23.590
<i>we'd return to a clean slate, 
and filming resumed.</i>

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:26.720
I'm finished with the stunt 
double's makeup and costume.

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:28.720
GoPro is ready.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.610
Projector is ready, as well.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:33.060
Attention!

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:38.860
After eloping with Katsuno, 
Mai attempts to return to her fiancé,

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:41.850
but she speeds off a cliff 
and meets her untimely demise.

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.890
It's the most spectacular 
scene of this movie.

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:46.900
Let's keep this tight!

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:48.180
Yeah!

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:50.380
Stunt double on standby.

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:55.210
This is the only day we're 
doing such an elaborate shoot.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:57.160
It's better than having 
to travel to a location.

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:58.630
We don't have the money for that.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:01.410
Do you have a minute?

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:02.850
What?

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:05.190
There's something I want to ask you.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.300
What is it?

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:09.380
This is called rear projection, right?

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:10.770
What about it?

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:15.950
Since the vehicle isn't actually moving, 
why do we need a stunt double?

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:23.580
You think I'd risk putting 
my lead actress in danger?

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.910
Danger? Where's the danger?

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.530
Aren't we just combining the actors' 
performance with a projected image?

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:30.660
Just shut up and watch this.

00:11:30.850 --> 00:11:31.840
Lights.

00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:33.520
Screen.

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:35.830
Projection, start.

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:38.210
Performance department, begin shaking.

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:41.500
Okada, keep your head down.

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:43.330
People will know you're a double.

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:46.070
Lights, begin shaking.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:53.650
Camera.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:54.750
Camera rolling.

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:57.430
Okay, action!

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:06.190
Pyrotechnics, are you ready?

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:07.370
Pyrotechnics ready.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:09.000
What are pyrotechnics?

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:12.920
Fire!

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:19.540
Mommy!

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:27.140
We got a great shot.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:31.080
But this just looks like 
Okada wearing a wig.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:33.950
We'll use digital synthesis to fix his face.

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:36.170
Where are we going to find 
the budget for that?

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:39.340
<i>And so, the second day of filming concluded.</i>

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:24.360
THIRD DAY OF SHOOTING

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:27.610
<i>Because Katsuno was stuck in a coma,</i>

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:32.680
<i>we began hastily filming scenes 
without Katsuno first.</i>

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:37.630
<i>Katsuno and Mai have eloped and 
greet the dawn at a motel.</i>

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:40.520
<i>Not wanting to be bothered by room service,</i>

00:13:40.520 --> 00:13:43.320
<i>Mai leaves the remains of her 
breakfast outside her door,</i>

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.980
<i>and a cat drinks milk from her dishes.</i>

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:53.430
<b>Soft Skin</b>

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:53.160
Apparently, it's a recreation of a famous 
scene from Truffaut's <i>Soft Skin</i>.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.340
Is the cat on standby?

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:56.730
About that...

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.150
Is there a problem?

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.680
Well, actually...

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:02.230
My kitty Tamasaburo ran away.

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:03.480
He ran away?

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:06.370
He's a serial escape artist.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:09.210
Why did you cast that cat?

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:13.960
There isn't a pet owner who wouldn't 
want to see their own kitty in a movie.

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.650
Then take responsibility by finding him.

00:14:16.650 --> 00:14:17.910
I don't think that's possible.

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:20.940
Once he escapes, he doesn't 
return for a week.

00:14:20.940 --> 00:14:24.600
Why don't I take responsibility 
by cosplaying a cat instead?

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.730
My movie isn't a comedy.

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:28.530
Find a replacement cat immediately.

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:30.100
Just so you know—

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:33.860
You're here to tell me that we don't have 
the budget for a professional cat actor, right?

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:35.570
As long as you're aware.

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:37.570
Director, it's Kanbara-san.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:39.230
What about Kanbara?

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:41.900
He captured a potential replacement cat.

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:50.860
<i>Meet Mai</i>, scene unknown, 
cut number unknown. Take one.

00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:52.490
Action!

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:00.990
Go on, Micuras.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:03.550
Micuras, go. Micuras!

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:05.370
Cut!

00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:08.260
Take two.

00:15:08.550 --> 00:15:09.610
Action!

00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:20.760
Cut!

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:23.470
Director...

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:26.150
We'll keep filming until it drinks.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:58.130
<i>The cat never drank the milk, 
and the third day of filming concluded.</i>

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:26.420
FOURTH DAY OF SHOOTING

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:31.790
<i>On the fourth day of shooting,</i>

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:36.390
<i>we filmed the blood donation 
charity ball with the Dance Club.</i>

00:16:37.310 --> 00:16:40.200
<i>But Maki was under a lot of pressure.</i>

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:47.640
<i>A director's job is to answer questions.</i>

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:50.630
<i>To direct costumes and color.</i>

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:52.980
<i>To apply the finishing touches 
to props and makeup.</i>

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:57.330
<i>They answer 20—no, 30 or 
even 40 questions a day.</i>

00:16:57.730 --> 00:17:01.640
<i>It's not important whether the 
answers are right or wrong.</i>

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:04.790
<i>What's important is that they 
keep answering questions.</i>

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:06.800
This is a camera rehearsal.

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:08.670
Music on.

00:17:09.940 --> 00:17:12.000
Two, three. Okay.

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.050
Mai-sama!

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:19.760
Hey, Katsuno!

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:22.190
Sexual harassment king!

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:24.770
Out of the way!

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:37.180
He may be obsessed, but Katsuno's 
tenacity is exemplary.

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:43.430
However, after all the sedative I injected 
him with, he won't wake up for a week.

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:47.750
<i>However, Katsuno recovered by the next day.</i>

00:17:48.490 --> 00:17:50.650
We only have one day left.

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:52.970
But we're low on funds and understaffed.

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:55.160
If only we weren't working 
with that meathead.

00:17:55.160 --> 00:17:57.480
If only he'd died on the first day.

00:17:57.480 --> 00:17:59.720
Will saying that now fix anything?

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.620
We need constructive opinions.

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:03.690
What does that mean?

00:18:03.690 --> 00:18:06.800
Please don't go after each 
other with personal attacks.

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:11.110
The Seijumonji High School Cinema 
Club's honor is riding on this.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:16.670
Yeah, but...

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:17.140
You crying about it won't fix anything.

00:18:16.340 --> 00:18:19.220
Just listen to me!

00:18:19.220 --> 00:18:21.010
Why are you being so tyrannical?

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:23.570
You can't shoot a movie democratically!

00:18:23.570 --> 00:18:26.300
I'm sick of your principled nature!

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:28.520
Oh, come on!

00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:29.450
I hope you all die!

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:34.080
Die, die, die, die, die!

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:39.500
Whether we like it or not, 
we only have one day left.

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:43.470
We'll alter the final scene.

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:47.010
The Seijumonji High School Cinema Club's

00:18:47.010 --> 00:18:50.800
continued existence is riding 
on tomorrow's shoot!

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:57.360
FINAL DAY OF SHOOTING

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:04.740
Director. Director.

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:07.870
Director, we're on standby.

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:15.630
Mitsugu.

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:17.380
Don't turn around.

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:21.560
We're making a few changes 
to the final scene.

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:23.590
Take this.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:28.780
This isn't real, is it?

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:33.070
Of course it's a film prop, idiot.

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:36.170
You know how to use it, right?

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:37.060
This is a take.

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.260
This is a take.

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:04.380
A-A Government?!

00:20:04.880 --> 00:20:07.320
The new night school student 
is the leading lady.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.350
Shockingly, Masumi Katsuno 
is playing opposite her.

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:11.750
That gorilla from the Karate Club?

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:13.060
Apparently, he paid for the 
entire budget himself.

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.570
I heard the shoot was incredible.

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:14.640
Start the movie already.

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:16.400
Don't shout. The fire station will show up.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:18.020
No, the police!

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:21.280
<b>Blood Donation Club and Cinema Club
First Joint Production</b>

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:30.910
<b>Meet Mai</b>

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:30.910
<b>Censored</b>

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:27.650
No objections!

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:29.480
We've been waiting for you, Mai-chan!

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:41.110
Katsuno-senpai of the Blood Donation Club.

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:43.790
Allow me to introduce our new member Mai.

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:46.200
Take this!

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:47.800
I'm taking you with me!

00:20:47.810 --> 00:20:49.970
<b>Censored</b>

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:38.550
Where the hell is Maki?!

00:21:38.550 --> 00:21:40.560
She fled a while ago.

00:21:46.480 --> 00:21:50.670
<i>A movie director must not fear failure.</i>

00:21:51.150 --> 00:21:54.640
<i>They need an indomitable spirit that 
can get up after countless setbacks.</i>

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:59.790
<i>Because that is what's 
demanded of a director.</i>

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:59.990
<b>Episode 8 "Looong story..."</b>

00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:49.490
Everyone has a secret.

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:53.480
Naturally, I am no exception.

00:23:53.820 --> 00:23:58.510
Nothing's more expensive than free, idiots.
